# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is the figure engine: the code that redraws the manuscript's
# figures, plus the derived tables it reads. The rule throughout is to ignore
# whatever a script in here can rebuild, and to keep whatever it cannot.
#
# These rules were written when this tree was a subdirectory of the analysis
# repository, and several paths still carried that `clean_repo/` prefix after it
# was split out. A prefixed rule matches nothing here, which silently dropped
# results/ and two FASTAs from every clone. Paths below are relative to this
# repository root; keep them that way.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Test, coverage and run artefacts
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml
.suite_logs/
*.log
slurm-*.out

# Editor and assistant scratch trees, ad-hoc throwaways
.gemini/
.claude/
delme*
test_label.png
test_custom_labels.png
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sequence data.
#
# GISAID-derived alignments must not be redistributed, so FASTA is ignored
# wholesale and the two small curated files the code opens by name are let back
# in one directory at a time. Both exceptions together come to 33 KB.
#
# Without them `git add` on those files silently succeeds and does nothing, and
# a fresh clone fails the tests that open NC_045512.2.fasta and the sK fixture
# alignment directly. Keep each path narrow, and keep what lands in them small.
#
# Note `*.fa` is deliberately NOT ignored: the per-lineage root sequences in
# data/roots/ use that extension and are inputs every figure needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fasta
!data/reference_genomes/*.fasta
!tests/fixtures/**/*.fasta

# Model weights and optimiser state, anywhere. No model is run from this
# repository, only its scored output; a checkpoint here is a mistake.
# (~180 GB of ESM-C checkpoints were once staged by a broad `git add` in the
# analysis repository, writing 137 GB of blobs into .git/objects.)
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.ckpt

# The exploration tree, kept out of the published repository. Its write-ups
# record dead ends and superseded runs, and nothing under results/ or output/
# depends on it.
dev/

# tools/build_figures.py builds here by default and compares the result with the
# shipped output/. It also holds every build's intermediates: build/panels/, the
# composite panels panelise.py places, and the per-step logs.
build/

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   results/  the derived tables every figure reads, about 26 MB. Ignoring these
#             leaves a fresh clone with nothing to draw from, and
#             tests/test_build_figures.py fails if a shipped input is ignored.
#   output/   the shipped figures, and the _values.tsv and _caption.md files a
#             rebuild is checked against.
#   figures/, data/  several panels cannot be regenerated from this repository
#             at all -- the Fig 1A tree, the Fig 1D heatmap and the Fig 2C epoch
#             plot have no generator. These are the only copies.
